  "reference_no_of_permission_being_relied_on": "Ref: 2014/1310\nApproved: 10/06/2014\nInternal refurbishment of the property including the replacement of the existing kitchen on the first floor; re-organising of the second floor moving partitions and installation of a new WC.\n\nRef: SOUTH/234/94/LB\nApproved: 16/03/1995\nVarious repair works\n",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development, by reason of the loss of original windows, would result in the unjustified loss of historic fabric to the detriment of the special character of the listed building. The proposal also fails to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the Kingsland Conservation Area. As such, the proposal is contrary to policies D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach), D4 (Delivering good design), and HC1 (Heritage conservation and growth) of the London Plan (2021) and policy LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character) and LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020) and the guidance contained within Hackney&#x27;s Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2025) and Retrofit SPD (2025)&lt;/p&gt;"
